From: plastron
Subject: [PATCH] devfreq: px30_dmc: switch the DDR in the vertical blank

Ask Rockchip's BL31 to switch the DDR rate in the display's vertical
blank, as Rockchip's own kernel does for every switch: the panel's kind
(SCREEN_MIPI, a DSI panel) and both wait flags in the page shared with
BL31. BL31 v1.37 (rkbin rk3326_bl31_v1.37) then waits for the VOP's line
flag 0, which the VOP driver puts at the end of the active area, unless
the display is off ("check_vop_en or pd_vo power_down break"), answers
PENDING when it has to wait and finishes from FIQ, which this driver
already handles with the complete interrupt.

The driver left them at 0 ("switching while the panel scans showed no
glitches"), so each switch stopped the DDR at any moment of the scan,
while the display read it. On ZyperOS the DDR switches every few seconds
in the menus (the launcher's idle ceiling) and around the in-game menu,
and one GKD Pixel 2 froze exactly there (2026-11-15).
---
diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c b/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
index e7e258c..2e13823 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@
 #define PX30_SHARE_PAGE_TYPE_DDR	2
 #define PX30_DRAM_GET_VERSION		0x08
 #define PX30_SET_RATE_PENDING		-6
+/* The panel's kind, for BL31's wait for the vertical blank: a DSI panel,
+ * Rockchip's SCREEN_MIPI (include/soc/rockchip/rockchip_dmc.h) */
+#define PX30_SCREEN_MIPI		7
 
 /* Start of the request page shared with BL31 */
 struct px30_dmc_params {
@@ -225,6 +228,19 @@ static int px30_dmc_set_rate(struct px30_dmc *dmc, unsigned long rate)
 {
 	struct arm_smccc_res res;
 
+	/*
+	 * The switch in the display's vertical blank, as Rockchip's own kernel
+	 * asks for every switch (rockchip_dmc.c sets the panel's kind and both
+	 * wait flags each time): BL31 waits for the VOP's line flag 0, which
+	 * the VOP driver puts at the end of the active area, unless the
+	 * display is off, and answers PENDING when it has to wait, then
+	 * switches from FIQ and raises the complete interrupt (below). Left at
+	 * 0, the DDR stopped for the switch at any moment of the scan, while
+	 * the display read it.
+	 */
+	writel(PX30_SCREEN_MIPI, &dmc->params->lcdc_type);
+	writel(1, &dmc->params->wait_flag0);
+	writel(1, &dmc->params->wait_flag1);
 	writel(rate, &dmc->params->hz);
 	res = px30_dmc_sip(PX30_SHARE_PAGE_TYPE_DDR,
 			   ROCKCHIP_SIP_CONFIG_DRAM_ROUND_RATE);
